# client-hangup.hex — the node hanging up an established call (RFC 5456 §6.2.5,
# notes §12 flow (d)). Hand-built from the RFC.
#
#        <== HANGUP      IAX 0x05 — NOT Control 0x01 (notes trap 18)
#   ACK  ==>             MUST, immediately; then the leg is destroyed
#
# Injected after client-connect.hex has brought the call up, so the peer's
# OSeqno is 2 (ACCEPT was 0, ANSWER was 1) and its ISeqno is still 1 — our only
# non-exempt full frame remains the NEW.
#
# Payload: CAUSE (0x16) "Bye", CAUSECODE (0x2a) 16 = normal call clearing
# (§8.6.21, §8.6.33).
8042 0001 00000190 02 01 06 05  16 03 427965  2a 01 10
